# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened in this workspace
# once already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a commit, and
# every checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# There is no build here. `run.sh` runs Vite, there is no `build` script, and a
# checked-in `dist` would be a second answer to "what does this page say" that
# disagrees with the first the moment somebody edits `src/`.
dist

# This app's own store: every question somebody wrote and every answer somebody
# gave, partitioned by project. It belongs to the machine the app runs on rather
# than to any repository this directory happens to be sitting in today. That is
# the whole of what "an app" means here — the directory can be copied to another
# machine, run, and be somebody's questions.
data
